WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:01.358
- So, you and I just met.

00:00:01.358 --> 00:00:01.869
- Yes.

00:00:01.869 --> 00:00:03.379
- And within 30 seconds you were willing

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:04.438
to give me your Netflix account.

00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:04.889
- Yeah, sure.

00:00:04.889 --> 00:00:06.218
- Let's do it.

00:00:06.218 --> 00:00:08.308
(energetic, trumpet music)

00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:11.175
- A recent study found
that 2/3 of Netflix users

00:00:11.175 --> 00:00:12.599
share their account with someone else

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:15.021
with nearly 20 percent of
people sharing their account

00:00:15.021 --> 00:00:17.278
with three people or more. Nuts.

00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:19.740
HBO's chairman and CEO famously said that

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.514
"[Password sharing] has no
impact on the business."

00:00:22.514 --> 00:00:25.359
So, password sharing, totally a thing.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:27.205
Until recently, I had been using my

00:00:27.205 --> 00:00:29.329
ex-roommate's ex-girlfriend's
Netflix password,

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.911
but I'm an adult, and it's
time to get my own passwords.

00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:35.582
So, I hit the streets of
Hollywood to ask people,

00:00:35.582 --> 00:00:37.324
"Yo, can I get your password?"

00:00:37.324 --> 00:00:39.042
Do you have Netflix?

00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:39.852
- Yes, indeed.

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:42.659
- Netflix, I have Hulu
Plus, I have Amazon Prime.

00:00:42.659 --> 00:00:43.804
- Yes, well, it's not mine.

00:00:43.804 --> 00:00:45.348
- It's not yours? What do you mean?

00:00:45.348 --> 00:00:46.764
- It's a friend's account.

00:00:46.764 --> 00:00:48.134
- You don't pay for it, you use...

00:00:48.134 --> 00:00:49.167
- I don't pay for it, no.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.642
- Is that your mother over there?

00:00:50.642 --> 00:00:51.350
- Yeah.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.178
- And you have no problem sharing

00:00:52.178 --> 00:00:53.478
these passwords with your son for free?

00:00:53.478 --> 00:00:54.312
- Not at all.

00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:55.379
- We also share it with my brother.

00:00:55.379 --> 00:00:56.216
- You share it with your brother?

00:00:56.216 --> 00:00:56.601
- And my mom.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.524
- And he doesn't pay anything.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.568
- Not at all.

00:00:58.568 --> 00:00:59.473
- Nothing, not a dime.

00:00:59.473 --> 00:01:00.194
- Not a cent.

00:01:00.194 --> 00:01:01.819
- Do you have a problem sharing
your password with people?

00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:02.655
- No.

00:01:02.655 --> 00:01:04.826
- It's no big deal, right? Password.

00:01:04.826 --> 00:01:06.614
I'm wondering, do you
think I could get on that?

00:01:06.614 --> 00:01:08.739
- My friend's?

00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:09.561
- Yeah.

00:01:09.561 --> 00:01:10.688
- Could you get on those accounts?

00:01:10.688 --> 00:01:11.363
- Yeah.

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:12.245
- I don't know you.

00:01:12.245 --> 00:01:13.066
- You don't know me.

00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:13.917
- No. I don't know you.

00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:15.879
- I'm going to turn to you.
Would you give me the passwords?

00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:16.831
- Are you going to pay?

00:01:16.831 --> 00:01:18.839
- You're not paying. Why should I pay?

00:01:18.839 --> 00:01:20.546
- But, I don't know your
mom, I don't know your dad.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.426
- Do you want to call my mom?
Do you want to call my mom?

00:01:22.426 --> 00:01:23.629
I will call my mom right now.

00:01:23.629 --> 00:01:24.702
- Because, I mean, if
I'm going to give you

00:01:24.702 --> 00:01:27.325
something personal like
that, my password...

00:01:27.325 --> 00:01:28.431
- I should, like, take you out to dinner

00:01:28.431 --> 00:01:29.381
in exchange or something.

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:29.628
- Exactly.

00:01:29.628 --> 00:01:31.056
- Unfortunately, we
don't have it memorized.

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:32.345
Yeah, I think it's a pattern.

00:01:32.345 --> 00:01:34.016
- Oh, I think I know. I think I know.

00:01:34.016 --> 00:01:34.806
- You know it?

00:01:34.806 --> 00:01:35.398
- Yeah.

00:01:35.398 --> 00:01:36.396
- Yeah, if you wanted to.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.706
- Yeah, I would love to. I don't have one.

00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:39.229
Would you be willing to let me on it?

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:39.728
- Yeah.

00:01:39.728 --> 00:01:40.727
- I mean if you really want it.

00:01:40.727 --> 00:01:41.596
- Yeah, why not, right?

00:01:41.596 --> 00:01:42.817
Because there are only
three people in our family.

00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:43.862
- You have the information on you?

00:01:43.862 --> 00:01:44.442
- Yeah.

00:01:44.442 --> 00:01:45.533
- I gotta pen right here.

00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:46.602
So you just let anyone on it.

00:01:46.602 --> 00:01:47.847
- Yeah, I don't care.

00:01:47.847 --> 00:01:48.494
- You think you remember it?

00:01:48.494 --> 00:01:49.028
- Yeah.

00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:49.992
- This is your friend's account?

00:01:49.992 --> 00:01:50.619
- Yeah.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:52.224
- And your friend's not going to mind?

00:01:52.224 --> 00:01:54.450
- There's like so many
people on this account,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.605
I don't think she'll notice.

00:01:55.605 --> 00:01:56.569
- How's your day going?

00:01:56.569 --> 00:01:57.550
- Pretty good.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.165
- There it is.

00:01:58.165 --> 00:02:00.328
- Yeah, and then the password?

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:01.825
"Vodevodka.."

00:02:01.825 --> 00:02:02.966
- So to be clear, we just met.

00:02:02.966 --> 00:02:03.506
- Yeah.

00:02:03.506 --> 00:02:04.585
